 "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/6b4d617df080cef71cd8f4b041601cf47ce0edf3/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\nThose three reads are done. Offset seems to be 0-based: offset 0 started at line 1 and offset 3 started at line 4. Next I'll run the tests.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nThe causes are clear. The edit tool needs each file read first, so I'll read the remaining files.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThe whole suite passes now: `python3 -m unittest` runs 16 tests with no failures. Before the fix it ran 15 tests (6 failures, 4 errors), because `tests/test_search.py` couldn't be imported and showed up as one error instead of its two tests.\n\n**The three reads you asked for:**\n- **(a)** Reading `catalog/` returned a list of its files: `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py`, `text.py`.\n- **(b)** Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135 of `books.py`.\n- **(c)** Offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 4\u20138. So `offset` counts from 0 and skips that many lines.\n\n**Fixes (only files in `catalog/` changed, no tests):**\n1. `search.py`: the import pointed at `catalog.nonexistent`; it now imports `normalize` from `catalog.text`.\n2. `books.py`: `parse_book` left the year as a string; it now converts it to an int with `int(year)`. That fixed both the year test and the `age()` test.\n3. `factory.py`: added the missing `Emma` book to `sample_books()`, which the docstring already listed.\n4. `fees.py`: the fee was `days_late + DAILY_FEE`; it's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n5. `inventory.py`: `recent(n)` returned one event too many (`[-n - 1:]`). It now returns `[-n:]`, and an empty list when `n <= 0`.\n6. `members.py`: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3 but the comment and tests say 5; it's now 5.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 9, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 90956, "requests_cache_write": 61512, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3871112, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 3064, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial29", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 297, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T08:03:10.327201+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 34.77, "t_checker_s": 0.177, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 3084, "tokens_cache_read": 90956, "tokens_cache_write": 61512, "tokens_fresh": 3066, "tokens_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_cache_read": 89924, "tokens_main_cache_write": 61512, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 3050, "tokens_output": 3064, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 90956, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 61512, "tokens_proxy_calls": 8, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 20, "toke